### 3. YANG Versioning Update
- **Presentation:** [05) Yang Versioning Update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-netmod-05-yang-versioning-update-00) (Rob Wilton)
- **Guidance Document:**
  - [draft-ietf-netmod-iana-yang-guidance](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-netmod-iana-yang-guidance/): Updated to reflect IESG approval and IANA registry handling without changing established processes. Jean Mahoney (RFC Production Center) requested that this document be held and published in the same cluster as the other three core versioning documents. Ready for Working Group Last Call.
- **Packages:**
  - [draft-ietf-netmod-yang-packages](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-netmod-yang-packages/): Replaced RFC 9195 JSON Instance Data document format with a dedicated JSON package definition file format. Updated compatibility rules to evaluate schema-level comparisons rather than individual module version numbers. Added off-device schema binding definitions.
  - Debate occurred between Rob Wilton, Joe Clark, and Ahmed Elhassany regarding the inclusion of module/package content hashes for local caching and validation.
- **Schema Comparison:**
  - [draft-ietf-netmod-yang-schema-comparison](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-netmod-yang-schema-comparison/): Clarified the distinction between locally resolved module comparison (used for determining semver updates for a single module in isolation) and fully resolved schema comparison (evaluating a compiled tree including all imported modules, augments, and deviations for package-level semver generation).

### 4. YANG Configuration Templates
